summary is: PC: Hi, I'm Matt Carter. Uh, I'm thirty two, and I'm in a private place, and I can have this conversation now.
Doctor: OK, Matt. So you mentioned you've been feeling tired, run down, and aching all over for the last six weeks, is that correct?
Patient: Yeah, that's right. Um, and, it's just, definitely the last six weeks, it might have been slightly longer than that, but it's just sort of that, feeling really tired, run down.
Doctor: OK, and you said you've been having some rashes as well, can you tell me a bit more about that?
Patient: Um, yeah, so I think it's, it's just, uh, on the back of my calf, I noticed this, uh, rash, uh, my wife noticed it actually, um, uh, it was quite, it was quite red, and, uh, sort of bumpy, like, uh, like a, like a, uh, a mosquito bite. Um, and it sort of, uh, came up, and then sort of, uh, disappeared after a couple of weeks, it was a pretty weird, but, yeah, it was quite, quite weird.
Doctor: And when did you first notice that rash?
Patient: Uh, probably around the end of February, the middle to end of Feb. And then it, like, it didn't actually cause too much itching, or anything, at the time. And, I, it faded over a couple of weeks, I guess.
Doctor: Do you remember where you got that from? Was it from a bite or anything?
Patient: Uh, I, I do quite a lot of walking, and we did, um, quite a lot while we were out in the, on holiday as well, but definitely, um.
Patient: Yeah, I mean, I don't, I don't recall any bugs, I don't remember seeing anything bitten but you often, like, yeah, as you're walking through, I was in shorts and boots but /
Doctor: OK. And whereabouts were you in the States?
Patient: Um, just sort of, um, he examined me, so.
Doctor: OK, and have you had any other symptoms, any headaches, blurred vision, tingling, numbness, anything like that?
Patient: Um, no.
Patient: But it's the sort of headache maybe in just generally feeling a bit crappy.
Doctor: And have you been able to go to work as usual?
Patient: Um, I've been going to work. I don't know how effective it's been. But, yeah, been, been.
Doctor: And what's your job?
Patient: Um, I work for a health technology company actually.
Doctor: OK, and has your concentration been affected, or your tiredness levels in the daytime at work?
Patient: Yeah, definitely sort of tired and, um, yeah, less energy, sort of probably than I, I would normally be.
Doctor: Have you been able to exercise OK?
Patient: Um.
Patient: Not as much. I, I don't know if it's, I haven't been able to or I've just been a bit lazy with it. I I'm not exercising as I would normally.
