summary is: {{ History : 
Patient is a 26 year old female
She has been stressed at work for few days
She has dry itchy skin over her arms and hands
She has used coconut butter for few days
She went swimming few days ago
She has no other fevers, vomiting or loose stools
She has no cough
She has no headache
She has no diarrhea
She has no chest pain
She has no abdominal pain
She has no back pain
She has no shortness of breath
She has no runny nose
She has no sneezing
She has no itchy eyes
She has no discharge from her eyes
She has no discharge from her ears
She has no discharge from her nose
She has no pain in her ears
She has no pain in her throat
She has no problem with her bowel and bladder
She has no problem with her waterworks
She is a teacher
She is not on any regular medications
She has a family history of asthma and hayfever
She is lactose intolerant
She does not smoke
She does not drink alcohol
She does not take recreational drugs
She lives alone at home
Plan:
Advise patient to use emollients and steroid cream
Advise patient to use antihistamines if needed
Advise patient to take paracetamol if she feels pain
Advise patient to come back in a week if symptoms do not improve
Advise patient to read the attached leaflet about dermatitis }}<|eot_id|>
