summary is: {{ PC: 64-year-old male, smoker, living with wife, working in a factory. 
HPC: 5-day hx of dry cough, SOB, myalgia, headache, fever (no temp taken), night sweats. No sputum production. No chest pain. 
PMH: Type 2 diabetes, high blood pressure, obesity.
DH: Metformin, lisinopril. 
SH: Lives with wife, works in factory. Smokes 4-9 cigarettes per week, drinks 4 pints of alcohol per week. Trying to cut down with e-cigarette. 
Imp: Upper respiratory tract infection, possible early flu. 
Plan: Advised to rest, drink plenty fluids, take paracetamol for fever. To review in 48 hours if no improvement. If SOB persists, to start antibiotics. }}<|eot_id|>
