He's got no previous history of this. He's not had any trauma to his neck, or any neck surgery. 
He's got type two diabetes, high blood pressure, on metformin, losartan and amlodipine. 
He's got a family history of heart disease. 
He's a non smoker, drinks alcohol socially. 
He's normally independent, lives alone, but he's not having any other symptoms, no headache, no vomiting, no visual disturbance, no visual disturbance. 
Imp: Acute left sided M.I. 
Plan: Ambulance called, and patient was assessed by the stroke doctor at the hospital. }}<|eot_id|>
processing idx: 19
len of response is: 19730
len of summary is: 9228
summary is: {{ 1/10
Headache has been going on for 3 days, over all over head, right eye more than left
Dull in nature, sometimes sharp, has developed over time
Has tried ibuprofen 3 x 200mg, no relief
Has been off work due to headaches
Visual disturbance (light sensitivity)
Nausea
No vomiting
No neck pain or stiffness
No difficulty with speech
No weakness in arms and legs
No rashes
No fever
No recent head injury
No previous similar episodes
No other medical history
No allergies
Lives with housemates
Works in IT, has had to reduce screen brightness
No recent eye tests
Smokes and drinks socially
Has family history of migraines in mother and sister
Wants to know what can be done to treat headache
Wants to know if migraine is genetic
Wants to be able to go back to work
Worried about impact on work and family
Plans to take naproxen
Wants to keep headache diary
Wants to come back in 1-2 weeks
Will phone if vision or weakness develops, or feeling unwell
